# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_config_bareword_precision.py" "CONFIG BARE-WORD PRECISION GATE: PASS" "config bare-word false-coupling precision (recall-safe)" "config bare-word precision: the CONFIG graph couples files that read the SAME config key (a real coupling), but the prior key-minting floor (len>=6) minted EVERY bare single word as a config_key -- so a dictionary/programming word that happens to be a key in SOME config file (module in tsconfig, dotenv in pyproject, public/metadata in a manifest) ALSO matched ordinary code occurrences (import from 'module', type='module', load_dotenv, a Postgres 'public' schema literal) and coupled files sharing NO real config resource. MEASURED on flask/httpx/zustand/axios + Veripsa: dropping bare-word keys removed 21 spurious file-pairs (worst: 'module' = 13 false pairs across axios+zustand) and 0 real ones. The fix (_cg_config._is_distinctive_config_key): a config key is coupling-bearing only with DISTINGUISHING STRUCTURE -- a COMPOUND (separator . _ - or a camelCase boundary) OR an ALL-CAPS ENV-VAR name; a bare single lower/Capitalized word has none, so it is not minted (no node -> no reads_config edge -> no spurious pair). This is the single-token generalization of the existing ubiquitous-key demotion. RECALL IS SACRED -- re-measured 0 real pairs lost: every genuine key (VERIPSA_DSN / GH_WEBHOOK_SECRET / payment_gateway_url / pull_requests / every env var) is compound or ALL-CAPS and is KEPT with identical reader counts. content-free (key NAMES only). This gate LOCKS both halves on synthetic configs+code (no DB, deterministic): the predicate contract, the 'module'/'dotenv'/'public' false couplings NOT forming, specific compounds + ALL-CAPS env-vars STILL coupling their readers, and a mixed file coupling via the SPECIFIC key only" "config precision: a bare single dictionary/programming word minted as a config_key (module/dotenv/public) created spurious file couplings on coincidental code occurrences -- measured 21 false pairs across 5 repos; now only compound or ALL-CAPS env-var keys are minted (0 real recall lost, every env var + compound kept); recall-safe, content-free" 8
